# Snippet Rules

496 snippets across 6 VS Code language scopes. Catalog is source; `snippets/*.code-snippets` is generated.

## Catalog layout

- **Manifest**: `src/snippets/catalog/index.js` — register every module in `CATALOG`.
- **Hand-authored**: `react-components.js`, `react-hooks.js`, `javascript.js`, `typescript.js`, `html.js`, `css.js`, etc.
- **Synced** (`synced: true`): originally from ES7+ extension, now vendored in-repo — prefer editing hand-authored modules; treat `components.js`, `hooks.js`, `redux.js`, etc. as legacy bulk sources.

## SnippetDefinition shape

```js
{
  key: "react-default-export-component",  // unique, kebab-case
  prefix: "rfcde",
  description: "React default export component",
  languages: ["javascriptreact", "typescriptreact"],
  body: ["line1", "line2"],               // string or string[]
  variants: {                             // optional per-language overrides
    typescriptreact: { body: ["…typed body…"] },
  },
}
```

## Authoring conventions

- **Tab stops**: `$1`, `$2`, … `$0` (final cursor). Use `${1:placeholder}` for named defaults.
- **TSX variants**: shared JSX body in `body`; typed props/types in `variants.typescriptreact`.
- **Prefixes**: unique per language after generation — build validation rejects duplicates.
- **Descriptions**: become VS Code snippet display names; keep concise and distinct.
- **Patterns**: prefer production-grade templates (AbortController fetch, accessible markup, typed reducers) matching existing catalog quality.

## Adding snippets

1. Add definitions to the appropriate catalog module (or create one and register in `index.js`).
2. Run `pnpm run build`.
3. Catalog must stay ≥ `MIN_SNIPPET_COUNT` (100); current count ~496.
